            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "When in visual mode, and is selecting a word for example, pressing ``sa`` triggers the keymap for mini.surround, and you are supposed to follow up with the surrounding character. And I tend to be pretty slow with my keymaps, so I have found that the follow up leaves barely any time for me to figure out the surrounding character before the sequence times out with this message: \"Messages: (mini.surround) Enter output surrounding identifier (single character) \". And I do not see any documentation on how to modify this behavior.\r\n\r\nMy mini.surround was set up as such.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n\t\trequire(\"mini.surround\").setup({\r\n\t\t\tsearch_method = \"cover_or_nearest\",\r\n\t\t\tn_lines = 20,\r\n\t\t})\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">When in visual mode, and is selecting a word for example, pressing <code class=\"notranslate\">sa</code> triggers the keymap for mini.surround, and you are supposed to follow up with the surrounding character. And I tend to be pretty slow with my keymaps, so I have found that the follow up leaves barely any time for me to figure out the surrounding character before the sequence times out with this message: \"Messages: (mini.surround) Enter output surrounding identifier (single character) \". And I do not see any documentation on how to modify this behavior.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">My mini.surround was set up as such.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"\t\trequire(&quot;mini.surround&quot;).setup({\n\t\t\tsearch_method = &quot;cover_or_nearest&quot;,\n\t\t\tn_lines = 20,\n\t\t})\n\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">\t\t<span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.surround<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n\t\t\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">search_method</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>cover_or_nearest<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,\n\t\t\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">n_lines</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">20</span>,\n\t\t})\n</pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "When in visual mode, and is selecting a word for example, pressing sa triggers the keymap for mini.surround, and you are supposed to follow up with the surrounding character. And I tend to be pretty slow with my keymaps, so I have found that the follow up leaves barely any time for me to figure out the surrounding character before the sequence times out with this message: \"Messages: (mini.surround) Enter output surrounding identifier (single character) \". And I do not see any documentation on how to modify this behavior.\nMy mini.surround was set up as such.\n\t\trequire(\"mini.surround\").setup({\n\t\t\tsearch_method = \"cover_or_nearest\",\n\t\t\tn_lines = 20,\n\t\t})",
